  "description": {
    "text": "Trainer Deck A, also called Brock's Deck, is a 60-card Fighting deck that Wizards of the Coast made in 1999 for the Pokémon League's Pewter City season. It was never sold: its box calls such decks tools for the Gym Leader, and they went to the first League leaders so they could play members. Few were handed out, and for a short time.\n\nThe cards are early Base Set printings with a red border and \"Trainer Deck A\" in red on the back. Their fronts match Base Set, except that the Machamp is non-holo and the only Base Set Machamp without the 1st Edition mark.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Trainer Deck A (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 28 August 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260828205617/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trainer_Deck_A_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Brock's Trainer Deck A and Misty's Trainer Deck B",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/brocks-trainer-deck-a-and-mistys-trainer-deck-b/13103"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "A red-bordered back reading \"Trainer Deck A\"",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Brock's Trainer Deck A and Misty's Trainer Deck B",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/brocks-trainer-deck-a-and-mistys-trainer-deck-b/13103"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Trainer Deck A (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 28 August 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260828205617/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Trainer_Deck_A_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
